## Diagnosis

The failure is a **compile error**, not an assertion failure:

```
tests/suite/multiply_test.go:13:14: undefined: calc.Multiply
FAIL	fixture/buildcodecompile/tests/suite [build failed]
```

`tests/suite/multiply_test.go` imports the production package
`fixture/buildcodecompile/services/calc` and calls `calc.Multiply(2, 3)`.
The production source `services/calc/calc.go` declares only `Add`; it
carries an explicit comment saying `Multiply` is the planted defect and
that the suite's package does not compile until it is declared.

Because Go builds a test package as a unit, the one missing identifier
takes down every test in `tests/suite` — `TestAddSumsItsArguments` and
`TestCanaryRecordsEachSuiteRun` never execute even though they would
pass. That is why the set reports as a single `<build>` group rather
than one failure per test.

So exactly one production symbol is missing. Nothing else in the fixture
is broken.

